    {
      "idx": 1,
      "label": "2",
      "overlay": 0,
      "note": "The chain now runs without hand-written code for a new family: proposer writes, verification accepts, a 0.6B caller trained on other families calls it. Stress the caveat: MRCR is a parsing task in disguise, so this is program discovery. The ladder: only the 8B with thinking succeeded, and on one seed in three; a single success is a sample, not a capability."
    },
    {
      "idx": 2,
      "label": "3",
      "overlay": 0,
      "note": "Generated families give resolution MRCR cannot: 37 held-out families per proposer. Thinking and scale both matter. Training the 4B works: SFT on the 8B's verified code transfers parsing to new string formats, and 40 steps of RL with the verified teaching score as reward lift held-out discovery from 9 to 30 of 74 attempts (p < 0.001), close to the 8B on string formats. It does not reach MRCR. The semantic families are capped by the helper's labelling accuracy, not the proposer."
    },
    {
      "idx": 3,
      "label": "4",
      "overlay": 0,
      "note": "The cleanest result of the day. Same code, four docstrings. The usage line alone carries the effect. The practical rule: every library ships with a usage line; the bootstrapper now inserts one. The deeper point: an untrained caller reads documentation, a distilled caller has learned the call."
    },
    {
      "idx": 4,
      "label": "5",
      "overlay": 0,
      "note": "MuSiQue is where the routine needs helper calls. The two-round library wins on accuracy and cost through the 0.6B caller. Everything that adds capacity elsewhere (recursion, bigger reader, more samples) does not help. The gap to gold paragraphs (about 0.2) is evidence selection."
    },
    {
      "idx": 5,
      "label": "6",
      "overlay": 0,
      "note": "LongBench-v2 is the external-validity check. The first generic library (map-reduce notes) tied direct reading at nine times the cost; a retrieval library (BM25 over passages for the question and each option, one read) beats direct reading by 0.11 at a quarter of its tokens. The lesson matches MuSiQue: choose evidence, do not summarize everything. Two earlier readings were withdrawn after fresh samples. The method lessons are the ones that cost most: scripted harnesses that did not match the kernel, verification sets that did not span deployment lengths."
    },
    {
      "idx": 6,
      "label": "7",
      "overlay": 0,
      "note": "The sharpened thesis in one breath, then the four next steps. If time is short, skip the list and ask the advisor which of the four matters most for the thesis."
    },
    {
      "idx": 7,
      "label": "8",
      "overlay": 0,
      "note": "For questions only."
